  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers IETF SCITT (Supply Chain Integrity, Transparency and Trust): the RFC 9943 architecture with Issuers, Signed Statements as COSE_Sign1 with CWT Claims iss and sub, Transparency Services, Registration Policies, append-only Verifiable Data Structures, Receipts and Transparent Statements, with RFC 9942 COSE Receipts as a dependency, and SCRAPI, the SCITT Reference API, pinned to draft-ietf-scitt-scrapi-11 with a build posture. It lists two families: architecture (RFC 9943 current; drafts -05 to -22 and -04 and earlier legacy) and scrapi (draft-11 current; drafts -04 to -10 and -03 and earlier legacy), with upgrade checklists. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, architecture and registration, message formats, the HTTP API, and verification and auditing.",
